  "literary_context": "Luke presents Jesus’ synagogue reading in Nazareth early in his public ministry, followed by a divided response. Acts then uses synagogue encounters to show Paul reasoning from Scripture and some listeners responding while others oppose him. The repeated setting links teaching, interpretation, and public response across Luke and Acts.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Deuteronomy 6 connects covenant faithfulness with teaching Israel’s words in ordinary life. Luke 4 and Acts show Scripture being read and discussed in synagogue gatherings, extending the biblical picture into public communal settings. The cited passages support that comparison, but do not by themselves prove that synagogues originated as a response to exile or that they directly prepared Christian worship.",
